Core TerminologiesTable (Relation): A structured collection of data entries organized into vertical columns and horizontal rows.Row (Tuple/Record): A single, individual entry in a table representing a specific entity.Column (Attribute/Field): A vertical entity in a table containing specific information or attributes for each record.Cardinality: The total number of rows present in a table.Degree: The total number of columns present in a table.Domain: The set of all unique, allowable values that a specific column or attribute can accept.
